     "You need a shell, and there is nothing wrong with that. The question this year is where to keep it. Colleagues who see you more may also ask more: how your mother is, whether the separation is final, why you left early on Thursday. Decide in advance what work gets to know. A short, friendly line you have practised, followed by a question back, does more than a wall. A shell you can close at half past five is what makes going back on Monday possible.",
     "The Moon is your planet, and its phases give you a rhythm of your own, so a few of them are worth marking. The new moon of January 7 and the new moon of December 27 both fall in Capricorn, your 7th house of close partners, the person who sees you without the work face. Together they frame the year with the same question: who gets you when the job is done? The new moon of July 4, at 11 degrees of Cancer, is your private new year, and Mercury turns direct on the same day. The full moon of July 18, in Capricorn at 25 degrees, comes with a penumbral eclipse so faint, and below the horizon in Europe, that you would never know. Its question is a plain one: who at home has been paying for your visibility?",
     "There is no full moon in Cancer at all in 2027, a small fact worth enjoying. Nothing in the sky insists on lighting you up in your own sign. In a year when your office may do that often enough, you are allowed to take it as permission to stay in."
