     "When you finish work, write a handover note as if a stranger were taking over your job tomorrow morning. Three lines at most: what got done, what is waiting, what can wait. Then close the laptop, hang up the apron or lock the van. If your work is caring for someone or running a house, the note still counts, and so does the moment you put it down. The idea is that work stops at the door instead of following you into the kitchen.",
     "Start at the new moon of January 7, and keep the notes in one place. Read a week's worth at the new moon of July 4, and you may see which worries turn up every single day. Those are the ones to raise with someone at work. The rest tend to stay on the paper, where they belong."
