     "Jupiter in your sign tends to feel like being slightly larger than life: more invitations, more appetite, a sense that doors open if you lean on them. The interesting part of 2027 is watching what stays once it has gone. Until April 13 Jupiter is retrograde, moving back from 26 degrees of Leo to 16, so the early months are for checking what this phase has actually given you. Make the list. Leave out the compliments and count the real things: the friend who stayed, the skill you now have, the project that exists outside your head.",
     "On April 3 and again on July 12, Jupiter forms an exact trine to Saturn in your 9th house of belief, study and long-distance plans. Those two days suit a commitment that outlasts the mood, such as enrolling on the course or saying out loud what you stand for. Saturn is the slower partner in that pair, and it likes a signature.",
     "When Jupiter moves on, it lands in your 2nd house, the part of your chart that deals with money and what you feel you are worth. Confidence stops being something other people hand you and becomes something you check privately: what you charge, what you keep, what you still need applause to believe. You may find a plain number on a page steadies you more than you expected. The Sun, your own planet, enters Leo on July 23, three days before Jupiter goes, so the handover happens in your birthday month, with everyone looking.",
