     "It marks a change of direction, and it does not ask you to do anything dramatic. Mercury enters Leo that same day and leaves on August 17, which makes this exact fortnight a good one for thinking and talking about what comes next. The second eclipse closes the window: the lunar eclipse of August 17 falls in your 7th house, faint and below the horizon in Europe. Two small tasks may help. On the day of the solar eclipse, write one line about what you want to begin for yourself. At the lunar one, ask what that line would cost the person next to you. Keep the big decisions for after the fortnight."
