     "Your best career stretch runs from late April to early June. The new moon of May 6 falls at 15 degrees of Taurus in your 10th house, which covers your job and how you are seen, and Venus stays there from May 14 to June 8. Apply, pitch, ask for the meeting. Saturn and Neptune in your 9th house add a long view: a qualification, work abroad, a belief about what your job is for. Neptune can make a distant option look better than it is, so check the details on any plan that sounds perfect. Daily work gets busier when Mars and Venus both enter your 6th house on November 25.",
     "Money shifts from noisy to steady. Mars in your 2nd house until February 21 and again from May 14 to July 15 can make spending quick and costs sudden, so leave a day between seeing and buying. From July 26 Jupiter takes over the same house, and it tends to make you think bigger about what you could earn. Thinking bigger is fine. Keep the figures on paper, review them around the new moon of August 31, and talk it through with someone who has no reason to flatter you. The full moon of November 14 in your 10th house is a good date to see whether your income and your reputation have started to match."
